# whale.grid v3 - the Codewhale whale, written by hand. One character is one cell, '.' is empty.
# Format (shared with whale-girl.grid; one parser, sprites/render.py, reads both):
#   ink <key> <theme token> <fill|open>   fill/open is the one-colour terminal level
#   sprite <name> <w>x<h>                 then exactly <h> rows of exactly <w> characters
#   stage <body> <w>x<h>                  the fixed canvas a body is composed onto
#   slot <body> <slot> <x> <y>            where a layer attaches, in stage cells
#   pose <body> <pose> <layer>[@<slot>] ... layers drawn in order; no slot means 0,0
# A layer named "x" with sprites x.0, x.1 ... is animated: frames play in order, the still is the last.
# v3: hero ringed in the shared line ink (42x37); wrench mirrored; ask glyph recentred; bubble frames
#     start at two bubbles; mark-14 favicon cut; zzz-hero; hero ships rest, done, sleep only;
#     whale-eye folded into line, whale-belly into the shared cream.
ink B whale fill
ink L whale-lite fill
ink D whale-deep fill
ink W cream open
ink P whale-pleat open
ink E line open
ink K line fill
ink S whale-lite fill
ink T text fill
ink O panel open
ink A warn fill

sprite mark 16x14
